{
  "reason": "Modify only model_design because SASRec.ranking_loss contains the recency weighting and per-history normalization targeted by the initial plan. Current macro validation HR@10 is 0.5037 versus baseline 0.505, with Electronics declining from 0.42 to 0.38; exponential weighting may suppress useful earlier supervision, but these results do not establish causality. Similar uniform-weight experiments have mixed outcomes, and failed objective substitutions support isolating this weighting change while preserving the existing architecture and sampled-softmax objective.",
  "module": [
    "model_design"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "In SASRec.ranking_loss(self, seq, pos, negatives, excluded), replace weights = torch.exp2((selected.float() - (pos.shape[1] - 1)) / 8.0) with weights = torch.ones_like(selected, dtype=torch.float32), retain weights = weights[keep], and update the loss comment to describe uniform transition weighting while preserving all existing variable names and function signatures. Preserve unreduced cross-entropy, float32 owner-indexed scatter_add_ reductions into loss_sums and weight_sums, denominator safeguards, and averaging over eligible histories so every selected valid transition has equal influence within its history and each eligible history retains equal aggregate influence; keep the random selection of at most 24 transitions unchanged. Keep unchanged the SASRec backbone, jointly trained history pooling and gate, normalized scoring, learned scale and item bias, prefix augmentation, 256-negative sampling and exclusion masks, optimizer, learning-rate schedule, batch settings, MAXLEN, dropout, SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, time limits, validation cadence, stopping, and single-checkpoint selection. Keep unchanged the supplied splits with preprocessing seed 0, training and evaluation seed 42, and pinned host validation using 200 users per category and 99 unique negatives; assess macro HR@10 and category results against 0.5037, treating the proposed 0.005–0.015 gain as an unverified hypothesis given the mixed historical outcomes. Retain DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four categories and routing, trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution and the shared search budget, and unchanged write_predict_script and prediction interfaces because inference is unchanged; train exactly one independent model from scratch per category and load exactly one selected checkpoint per category, without ensembles, averaging, separately fitted scores, other-trial checkpoint reuse, extra datasets, pretrained weights, hidden-test access, or evaluator changes.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
